."\n```\n\n**4. `/tmp/movie-recommender-mcp-temp/movie-reccomender-mcp/mcp.yaml`**\n```yaml\nstartCommand:\n  type: stdio\n  configSchema:\n    type: object\n    properties: {}\n  commandFunction: |\n    (config) => ({ command: \'python\', args: [\'-m\', \'server\'] })\nexampleConfig: {}\n```\n\n**5. `/tmp/movie-recommender-mcp-temp/movie-reccomender-mcp/Dockerfile`**\n```dockerfile\nFROM python:3.11-slim\n\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY . .\nRUN pip install -r requirements.txt\n\nCMD ["python", "server.py"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Installation and Running Instructions\n\nBased on the configuration files found, there are two ways to run this project:\n\n### Option A: Docker\nBuild and run using the provided Dockerfile:\n```bash\ncd /tmp/movie-recommender-mcp-temp/movie-reccomender-mcp\ndocker build -t movie-recommender-mcp .\ndocker run movie-recommender-mcp\n```\n\n### Option B: Direct Python\nInstall dependencies and run directly:\n```bash\ncd /tmp/movie-recommender-mcp-temp/movie-reccomender-mcp\npip install -r requirements.txt\npython server.py\n```\n\nOr via the MCP protocol (as specified in `mcp.yaml`):\n```bash\npython -m server\n```\n\n### Dependencies\nThe project requires Python and these packages:\n- `requests` -- HTTP library for calling the TMDb API\n- `mcp` -- Model Context Protocol SDK (FastMCP framework)\n- `requests-cache` -- Caching layer for HTTP requests\n- `retry-requests` -- Retry logic for failed requests\n\n### Notes\n- The project is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides movie recommendations via the TMDb API.\n- It exposes a single tool called `get_movies` that takes a keyword string and returns up to 3 movie suggestions.\n- The TMDb API key is hardcoded in `movie_recommender.py` (the comment says it can be replaced with a real key).\n- There is no `setup.py`, `pyproject.toml`, or `package.json` file -- installation is handled solely through `requirements.txt` and `pip`.'}]
