onfig_validation {id}_{owner}_{name}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Validation Process\n\nThe tool uses an `MCP_Client` class (at `/home/silimon/mcp-auto/MCP-Auto-Server/src/MCP_Client.py`) that supports three transport types:\n\n| Transport Type | Config Fields Required | Description |\n|---------------|----------------------|-------------|\n| `stdio` | `command`, `args`, `env`, `cwd` | Spawns a local subprocess |\n| `sse` | `url`, optional `headers`, `command`, `args`, `env`, `cwd` | Server-Sent Events connection |\n| `streamable_http` | `url`, optional `headers`, `command`, `args`, `env`, `cwd` | HTTP-based streaming connection |\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- Sets清华源 (Tsinghua PyPI mirror) environment variables for Python package installs\n- For SSE/streamable_http with a `command` field, it starts a local server process and waits for the port to be ready\n- Calls `session.initialize()` then `session.list_tools()` to verify the server works\n- Reports `[OK]` on success with the list of tool names, or `[ERROR]` on failure\n- Properly cleans up server processes on failure\n\n---\n\n### Output Messages\n\n| Message | Meaning |\n|---------|---------|\n| `[OK] The server {name} started successfully, tools: {tool_list}` | Success - server connected and tools listed |\n| `[Warning] The server {name} started successfully, but no tools were found.` | Server started but exposes no tools |\n| `[WARN] The server {name} init cancelled` | Connection was cancelled |\n| `[ERROR] Failed to connect the MCP server: {error}` | Connection failed |\n| `The server {name} does not exist.` | Server name not found in config |\n| `Invalid config format.` | Config file is not valid JSON/dict |\n| `No server configuration found.` | No servers section found in config |\n\n---\n\n### Git History\n\nThe source has been modified across several commits:\n- `e431474` - Initial version (only supported `"Servers"` key)\n- `5283357` - Fixed validation (added key normalization, fallback parsing modes)\n- `5e5ee1b` - Bug fix for exp2'}]
